   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4f28a7a0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1a: Variable selection and sample restriction\n",
    "First we read in the monthly stock characteristics data and restricting the sample to observations dated on or after January 1, 2000."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "df981b05",
   "metadata": {
    "cache": false
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: false\n",
    "df = pd.read_parquet(\"//Users/AstridMoeller/AEF/data/stock_characteristics_monthly.parquet\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Reading in the file\n",
    "#| df = pd.read_parquet(\"/Users/esmeraldalarsson/Desktop/Advanced Empirical Finance/stock_characteristics_monthly.parquet\")\n",
    "df.head()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep observations from January 2000 onward\n",
    "df[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"date\"])\n",
    "df = df.loc[df[\"date\"] >= \"2000-01-01\"].copy()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "86e5c4c4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We select ten stock characteristics and four macro variables capturing key GKX themes and macroeconomic conditions, including valuation, interest rates, and credit risk."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "c532de0e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "stock_chars = [\n",
    "    \"characteristic_mom12m\",  # 12-month momentum\n",
    "    \"characteristic_mom1m\",   # Short-term reversal (replaces r2_1 — not in dataset)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_mvel1\",   # Size (log market cap)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_bm\",      # Book-to-market (value)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_roaq\",    # Return on assets (profitability)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_ep\",      # Earnings-to-price\n",
    "    \"characteristic_turn\",    # Share turnover (liquidity)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_beta\",    # Market beta\n",
    "    \"characteristic_invest\",  # Investment growth\n",
    "    \"characteristic_acc\",     # Accruals\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "macro_vars = [\n",
    "    \"macro_dp\",   # Dividend-price ratio\n",
    "    \"macro_ep\",   # Earnings-price ratio\n",
    "    \"macro_tbl\",  # T-bill rate\n",
    "    \"macro_dfy\",  # Default yield spread\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "base_cols = [\"permno\", \"date\", \"ret_excess\", \"mktcap_lag\", \"sic2\"]\n",
    "df = df[base_cols + stock_chars + macro_vars].copy()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9ca9ecb5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The selected characteristics are economically interpretable and widely used in asset pricing. In particular, mom12m, mvel1, bm, and roaq capture momentum, size, value, and profitability. These are complemented by variables reflecting valuation, trading activity, risk, investment, and accounting quality. The macro variables summarize market valuation, interest rates, and credit conditions, which are standard predictors of returns.\n",
    "\n",
