    "\n",
    "## Exercise 2\n",
    "\n",
    "### Exercise 2a: Model descriptions\n",
    "\n",
    "**Elastic Net** is a penalized linear regression model that combines the $L_1$ penalty from the Lasso and the $L_2$ penalty from Ridge regression. It minimizes the residual sum of squares subject to a penalty on coefficient size, which helps control overfitting in high-dimensional settings with correlated predictors. This is particularly relevant in our setting, as the feature matrix includes stock characteristics, interaction terms, and industry dummies. The key hyperparameters are the overall penalty strength (`alpha`) and the mixing parameter (`l1_ratio`), where `l1_ratio = 1` corresponds to the Lasso and `l1_ratio = 0` corresponds to Ridge.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Neural Network (MLP)** approximates $g(z_{i,t})$ as a composition of linear transformations and nonlinear activation functions across multiple hidden layers. Each neuron computes $x_k^l = f\\left(\\theta_0^k + \\sum_j z_j \\theta_j^k\\right)$, where $f$ is the ReLU activation function. The network is trained by minimizing the mean squared prediction error via backpropagation. The key hyperparameters are the number and size of hidden layers (`hidden_layer_sizes`), the $L_2$ regularization strength (`alpha`), and the maximum number of iterations (`max_iter`).\n",
    "\n",
    "Together, the two models provide a comparison between a structured, regularized linear benchmark and a more flexible nonlinear model.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Exercise 2b: Time-respecting data split"
